The model weights are downloaded at run time from the Hugging Face Hub
(chaoliangUNSW/Jev-Style-0.8B-Decision-v3 and its -MLX / -GGUF builds). They are a fine-tuned
derivative of Qwen3.5-0.8B (Copyright 2026 Alibaba Cloud, Apache-2.0); see the NOTICE file of each
model repository for the modifications.

The question types (choice / score / noul) and the request shape follow the public typed-decision
("systemone") convention so the same client code works against different servers.

Not affiliated with, endorsed by or connected to TypeSafe or Jev. "Jev-Style" only describes the kind
of model (a small typed-decision model in a similar style); no Jev weights, code or outputs are included.
Not affiliated with or endorsed by Alibaba Cloud / the Qwen team, the Laya authors, the Kev authors or the
JevK5 author.

The named cascade cascade-9b and jevk5: cascade tiers use JevK5-9B by alibiserikbay
(alibiserikbay/JevK5-9B, Apache-2.0) through its runtime jevk5 (github.com/allebee/jevk5, Apache-2.0).
Neither is included: the runtime is installed separately and the weights are downloaded at run time from
their own repository. Per its model card, part of JevK5-9B's training labels were generated by OpenAI's
GPT-6 Luna and are subject to OpenAI's terms. tests/conftest.py mirrors jevk5's question validation
(jevk5/server.py, v0.3.3, Apache-2.0) for its fake jevk5 module.

Web demos: see the LICENSES.md file inside each folder under jev_style/web/ for third-party data.
